## 6. Order of validation and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`

1. Spring Security `@PreAuthorize` role check (`OWNER_ADMIN`). Failure → `AccessDeniedException` → 403/entry point.
2. Request body deserialization + annotation-based Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@NotNull/@Pattern/@Size/@Email` etc.). Failure → `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (advice lines 133-154). This happens BEFORE the controller body.
3. Controller body runs, in code order (lines 119-163):
   a. Map DTO → `Owner` (no id).
   b. Normalize address; empty → 400.
   c. If email present: lowercase + regex check; invalid → 400.
   d. Postcode-vs-city/region check; invalid → 400.
   e. Normalize telephone to E.164; invalid → 400.
   f. Resolve registration date (default now, roll to business day).
   g. Per-day cap: `countOwnersRegisteredOn(date) >= 100` → 429 (each such helper calls `findAllOwners()` in its own read-only tx).
   h. Compute identity key; `isDuplicate` → 409.
   i. Per-city cap: `countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` → 409.
   j. `assignRegistrationAttributes` (customerCode, membershipNumber, householdId, namesakeCount, householdMemberCount) — computed from the current owner population, so must run before save while counts still exclude this owner.
   k. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — opens a read-write transaction, `ownerRepository.save` → JPA persist; entity-level Hibernate constraints (`Owner`/`Person` `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern`) validated at flush/commit; DB assigns id. Constraint/DB failure surfaces via the advice (500 or, for `DataIntegrityViolationException`, 404).
   l. AUDIT log line (success only).
   m. Map entity → `OwnerDto`, set `bulkSignupWarning` (another `findAllOwners()`), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.
   n. Return 201 CREATED with the `OwnerDto` body.
